            <div xml:id="d465">

                <pb facs="0562" n="464" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg464"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/3461: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Hankow (Adams) to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-01-08T12:00:00+08:00">January 8,
                        1932—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 5:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3. Communists are heavily attacking Hwangpei city 20 miles north of Hankow.
                    Although Shekow, 10 miles north of Hankow, is protected by strong military
                    trenches, I have, as a precautionary measure, advised the American women and
                    children of the Lutheran Theological Seminary there to withdraw therefrom for a
                    few days. Legation and Nanking informed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Adams</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
